{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from obtuse-phenocryst-verdin. The shared git wrapper `run_git` in `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py` (the `subprocess.run` call at line 199 and the `subprocess.Popen` in `_run_in_group` at line 229) runs git with `text=True` and no `encoding`, and `ssh_keygen_version` in `src/rebar/attest/sshsig.py:58` runs `ssh -V` the same way. Python then decodes child output, and encodes `str` stdin, with the locale codec. On Windows that is cp1252, so non-ASCII git output (commit subjects, paths, ticket titles) that passes through `run_git` is garbled, or raises `UnicodeDecodeError` on the bytes cp1252 leaves undefined (0x81/0x8D/0x8F/0x90/0x9D). `run_git` is the wrapper that the store's locked git seam and its callers (for example `_snapshot/delta_tree.py`'s `checkout-index --stdin` path list) use, so this affects Windows users of the tracker, not only tests.\n\nReproduced on macOS at origin/main `1654f3e3e53`: under `python -X warn_default_encoding -W error::EncodingWarning`, `gitutil.run_git(None, \"--version\")`, `gitutil.run_git(None, \"--version\", timeout=5)` and `sshsig.ssh_keygen_version()` each raise `EncodingWarning: 'encoding' argument not specified`.\n\nNot every git read goes through `run_git`. An AST census of `src/rebar` finds 92 text-mode subprocess calls with no `encoding`, in 58 files. Examples are `_store/project_ensures.py:42` `_git`, `_store/footprint.py:158,295`, `_commands/verify_commit.py:141,146`, `_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:566`, `_engine_support/commit_impact.py:275` and `mirror_guard.py:230`. Those direct callers are **out of scope** here. obtuse-phenocryst-verdin owns the ones behind Windows-sweep failures, and the follow-up bug dogtired-blank-fieldmouse (linked `discovered_from` this ticket) owns the remainder plus a guard against new ones. This ticket fixes the 3 sites it names, so that the shared wrapper is correct for every caller that uses it.\n\n## Approach\n\nName the codec at each of the 3 sites, so neither decoding nor stdin encoding depends on the host locale:\n\n- `run_git` and `_run_in_group`: pass `encoding=\"utf-8\" if text else None` and `errors=\"replace\" if text else None`. git writes data (log output, paths, object content) as UTF-8 by default, so UTF-8 is the right codec. The `encoding` also governs text-mode `input_data`, so `str` stdin is encoded as UTF-8 too. That matches what git expects for path lists such as `checkout-index --stdin`. The conditional is required: `subprocess` switches to text mode whenever `encoding` or `errors` is set, so passing them unconditionally would break the `text=False` binary contract documented in `run_git`'s docstring (gitutil.py:177-181).\n- Why `errors=\"replace\"` rather than strict: `subprocess` applies one codec and one error handler to both stdout and stderr, and git translates its stderr messages through gettext in the user's message locale. Under a legacy non-UTF-8 locale, or with a non-default `i18n.logOutputEncoding`, strict decoding would turn a readable git diagnostic into a `UnicodeDecodeError` that hides it. With `replace`, a byte that is not UTF-8 decodes to U+FFFD and the call never raises because of decoding. Correct UTF-8 output, which is git's default for data, decodes identically under either handler. This is the chosen disposition for undecodable output: lossy replacement, never an exception.\n- `ssh_keygen_version`: pass `encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"`. The output is a version banner that is only matched by `_VERSION_RE`.\n\nThis adds no config key, env var or flag. It is portable: an explicit codec is the platform-neutral form. It removes the locale as an input and uses no POSIX-only API.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py`: `run_git` and `_run_in_group` pass the encoding and error handler.\n- `src/rebar/attest/sshsig.py`: `ssh_keygen_version` passes them.\n- `tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py` (new): regression tests.\n- Out of scope: the other direct text-mode subprocess callers listed above, owned by obtuse-phenocryst-verdin and dogtired-blank-fieldmouse.\n\n## Testing\n\n`tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py`. The minimum Python is 3.11 (`pyproject.toml` `requires-python`), so `-X warn_default_encoding` is always available. Each case runs in a child interpreter (`sys.executable`, the same venv and editable install) started with `-X warn_default_encoding -W error::EncodingWarning`. The child prints `ascii()` of its result, and the parent asserts both the child's exit code 0 and the printed value:\n- `run_git(<tmp repo>, \"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%s\")` without a timeout returns the non-ASCII subject `\"café ✓\"`;\n- the same call with `timeout=30` (the `_run_in_group` path) returns the same subject;\n- `run_git(<tmp repo>, \"hash-object\", \"--stdin\", input_data=\"café ✓\\n\")`, through both the no-timeout and the `timeout=30` path, returns the same object id as `git hash-object` over the UTF-8 bytes of that text (stdin is encoded as UTF-8);\n- `run_git(..., text=False)` still returns `bytes` (edge case: binary mode stays binary, and this case also passes on the pre-fix code);\n- `ssh_keygen_version()` completes without the warning (skipped when `ssh` is not on PATH, because the `FileNotFoundError` path never decodes).\n\nRED check: write the test file first in the worktree and run `pytest tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py` before editing `src/`. Every case except the `text=False` one must fail, with the child's stderr naming `EncodingWarning`. Then apply the fix and rerun.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Before the `src/` edit, `pytest tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py` fails every case except `text=False` with `EncodingWarning` in the child's stderr. The failing output is recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [x] After the fix, `pytest tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py` passes.\n- [x] `make verify` passes.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795077658250606620,"uuid":"62cb61a1-63f3-4cd7-b4fd-dfe399734731"}